{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "001D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "TEXTIT_0001": "{\\it subcategory}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{categories-definition-subcategory}\n", "suffix": "\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ddaeadfb966b317bbee4043fbcc7a23a27c94b4c390834c9ca3b1ca4a24c069a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c29f8207be0a1c431fe7a4489b1157ee35a54cc0ab1317136c095537cf8698ad", "source_text": "A <TEXTIT_0001> of a category <MATH_0001> is a category <MATH_0002> whose objects and arrows form subsets of the objects and arrows of <MATH_0003> and such that source, target and composition in <MATH_0004> agree with those of <MATH_0005> and such that the identity morphism of an object of <MATH_0006> matches the one in <MATH_0007>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ba0f20761ecdc6ceb20e68b0fc6316f59a0c08b5d9d9d49915834d3db4b88320", "unit_id": "tag:001D:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "001D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Mor_\\mathcal{A}(x, y) = \\Mor_\\mathcal{B}(x, y)$", "MATH_0004": "$x, y \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{A})$", "TEXTIT_0001": "{\\it full subcategory}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0d31f70ee3725cbda8937b92da2f8737801138ac55d15be012ff33742c6e69cd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1310cd9ef81af4fd424abb56ae5ed9a7b2fdadfaf37ddb53c05dd0c05edb01a7", "source_text": "We say <MATH_0001> is a <TEXTIT_0001> of <MATH_0002> if <MATH_0003> for all <MATH_0004>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3768ba1fd97beb504528ee90f5172935701fcbb2f2f9cc4b3b0edbb3fcda062f", "unit_id": "tag:001D:p001"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "001D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0003": "$x \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{A})$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0005": "$x$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "TEXTIT_0001": "{\\it strictly full}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{definition}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2c15eb0e14660349b509ca967d67ae3117a49dcc0503c8769e152b1a29811570", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fae9d607cac4e372b9b6d30d4078db3966812d4b9f333670ebe828e3c60dbc3c", "source_text": "We say <MATH_0001> is a <TEXTIT_0001> subcategory of <MATH_0002> if it is a full subcategory and given <MATH_0003> any object of <MATH_0004> which is isomorphic to <MATH_0005> is also in <MATH_0006>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6a0f4db34854f124d9dd910c8d6f5e6d06518b83c7f3132a39ce1e57a6bfd95f", "unit_id": "tag:001D:p002"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "001D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{A} \\subset \\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{A} \\subset \\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Ob(\\mathcal{B})$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\noindent\n", "suffix": "\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5816a14c5141d396ce988dfdc28dd3400586a4c0e4f2d6575ee6dcf4509338a6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1e4284c37c5eb0031d0556605a0446a792cfc3d99632c4b80ba32f9b9443b59a", "source_text": "If <MATH_0001> is a subcategory then the identity map is a functor from <MATH_0002> to <MATH_0003>. Furthermore a subcategory <MATH_0004> is full if and only if the inclusion functor is fully faithful. Note that given a category <MATH_0005> the set of full subcategories of <MATH_0006> is the same as the set of subsets of <MATH_0007>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:57fa9e66a91eb69bab973df032b5346378046ed7fd9178573686faf4cab288b0", "unit_id": "tag:001D:p003"}
